{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfi6Gt3by4eb6Sq1aAbnu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ticket 03 is finished. `html` now returns an opaque `Markup` value instead of a string, and the output is byte-for-byte the same as before. All the required suites pass: `npm test` (181), `test:ssr` (60), `test:build` (33), `test:hydration` (33 + 17) and `typecheck:hydration`.\n\n[x] `html` returns a value typed `Markup` that is not assignable to `string` in the type tests\n[x] `String(html\\`...\\`)` equals the string the same call returned before this change\n[x] Markup interpolated into another `html` call is not escaped again\n[x] An array of markup in child position flattens as before\n[x] A render function that returns markup produces the same host HTML as one that returns the equivalent string\n[x] A declared string prop is still escaped exactly once\n[x] `npm test`, `npm run test:ssr`, `npm run test:build`, `npm run test:hydration`, and `npm run typecheck:hydration` pass\n\n**What changed:**\n1. In `src/htm.ts`, the old internal `_Trusted` class became the exported `Markup` class. `html`, `h` and `raw` all return it, and a component's render output is wrapped the same way.\n2. In `src/builders.ts`, a render function may return `string | Markup`. The static `render` converts the result and still returns a string. The core entry imports `Markup` as a type only, so it adds no runtime code.\n3. Callers that need a string now convert with `String(...)`: `example-hydration/server/app.ts` (the route bodies are now typed `Markup`), the `innerHTML` assignment in `client/index.ts`, and the existing templater tests in `test/index.ts`.\n4. I updated the line in `AGENTS.md` that said `html` returns a plain string.\n\n**Things outside the ticket you should know about:**\n- **Broken import, fixed:** `test/index.ts` imported `example-hydration/client/reveal.js`, which doesn't exist (`reveal` lives in `util.js`). That would have stopped `npm test` from typechecking even before my change, so I pointed the import at `util.js`.\n- **Lint, not fixed:** `test/plugins.ts`, which this ticket doesn't touch, has two existing unused-variable lint errors. I left them alone.\n- **One commit instead of one per item:** I made a single commit rather than one per checklist item. The return-type change breaks every caller at once, so the items couldn't pass separately."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":745,"cache_read_input_tokens":63830,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":745},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6553cfd8-b33b-4435-80e2-cb32d6fcd330","uuid":"16809400-8567-4f41-a380-ccc77c00bc6a","timestamp":"2026-10-04T23:49:04.128Z","request_id":"req_011Cfi6GsLvzFFdqV9hfMppF"}
